1
00:00:00,729 --> 00:00:04,168
So the task, the session that you just created was a vanilla

2
00:00:04,168 --> 00:00:05,368
Claude or Codex session.

3
00:00:06,168 --> 00:00:09,448
But we also have a concept of Unmute Agent.

4
00:00:09,528 --> 00:00:13,048
So Unmute Agent is a specialized session that we create

5
00:00:13,528 --> 00:00:16,489
and it has these tools and some capabilities

6
00:00:17,048 --> 00:00:18,969
that allows it to find tasks,

7
00:00:18,969 --> 00:00:21,969
allows to create new tasks and continue working on

8
00:00:21,969 --> 00:00:23,129
existing tasks for you.

9
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:26,599
So think of it like a task manager or a session manager.

10
00:00:26,998 --> 00:00:30,199
Let's say you were working on something a couple of days back

11
00:00:30,518 --> 00:00:32,679
and you want to start working on it again.

12
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:35,478
So what you could do is you can just unmute yourself.

13
00:00:35,478 --> 00:00:39,399
You can talk to Unmute Agent and you can tell it, hey, let's start,

14
00:00:39,478 --> 00:00:41,238
let's continue working on the landing page.

15
00:00:41,319 --> 00:00:41,959
That's it.

16
00:00:42,039 --> 00:00:43,719
That's the, you know,

17
00:00:43,798 --> 00:00:47,319
simplest of a request that you have to make to the Unmute Agent.

18
00:00:48,039 --> 00:00:50,598
What it will do is it will find the right session

19
00:00:51,018 --> 00:00:54,698
that you are already working on and it will resume that session.

20
00:00:54,859 --> 00:00:56,819
It will make sure that it has the right set of

21
00:00:56,819 --> 00:00:59,499
contexts and you can just proceed from there.

22
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:01,378
So it's like a sessions manager.

23
00:01:01,378 --> 00:01:05,379
It's really useful and you don't have to think about what session you

24
00:01:05,379 --> 00:01:06,299
were, you were working on earlier.

25
00:01:06,299 --> 00:01:07,739
You don't have to look for those sessions.

26
00:01:07,978 --> 00:01:08,539
At the same time.

27
00:01:08,539 --> 00:01:10,459
You can say, hey, can you do this,

28
00:01:10,709 --> 00:01:13,739
can you do this task A again for this particular thing?

29
00:01:14,138 --> 00:01:16,659
And it'll just make sure to find the right set of

30
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:18,379
context from your past session.

31
00:01:19,418 --> 00:01:22,379
Just bring that in front of you so you don't have to think about

32
00:01:22,698 --> 00:01:23,659
or worry about

33
00:01:24,328 --> 00:01:27,299
resuming a previous session, finding the right session, etc.

34
00:01:27,299 --> 00:01:29,338
So it's a really good, it's a really important feature.

35
00:01:29,659 --> 00:01:31,899
And yeah, think of it like a task manager.

36
00:01:32,138 --> 00:01:36,459
What you have to do is double tap the Right Command key to talk to

37
00:01:36,459 --> 00:01:37,259
Unmute Agent

38
00:01:38,138 --> 00:01:41,578
and just say out loud whatever you want to say.

39
00:01:41,578 --> 00:01:44,459
You can say the follow up message as shown here to test it

40
00:01:44,759 --> 00:01:47,438
and once done tap the Right Command key again and

41
00:01:47,438 --> 00:01:49,399
that will submit a Unmute Agent request.

42
00:01:49,748 --> 00:01:51,478
it will also pop up in a notch.

43
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:55,638
So you can just tap on the notch and it will just show Unmute

44
00:01:55,638 --> 00:01:59,078
Agent specific task or Unmute Agent specific chat box.

45
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:02,438
So that's a chat of yours and the Unmute Agent.

46
00:02:02,679 --> 00:02:05,308
And once the Unmute Agent is done with the follow up,

47
00:02:05,308 --> 00:02:08,038
it will most likely give you a link

48
00:02:08,359 --> 00:02:12,278
and you can tap that link and it will open the right session.

49
00:02:12,598 --> 00:02:13,919
So it's a really cool feature.

50
00:02:13,919 --> 00:02:14,838
You can just try it out.
